## Why this approach

The rule doc asks for element-specific **anatomy**, **forbidden patterns**, and **verification** without generic boilerplate. The KS contract template uses `## Anatomy`, `## Forbidden patterns`, and `## Deterministic checks` for verification; the shared `contract-specificity.mjs` logic already powers `check-visual-catalog.mjs`, so this check reuses that library instead of AI heuristics and stays deterministic and token-efficient.
